{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"unrelaxing-conclusive-sapsucker","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\n\nPreserve the reconciler's uncommitted inbound events and bridge-bot authorship before the raw workflow commit-back is removed. The push-only primitive from [rebar:953a-d616-52d3-4efe] cannot stage or commit a dirty tracker, and existing callers depend on that push-only contract.\n\n## Approach\n\n- Add `commit_and_push_tickets_branch(tracker, *, message, strict=False, author_name=None, author_email=None)` in `src/rebar/_store/push.py`.\n- Resolve the canonical tracker, then under its existing write lock inspect the dirty tree, stage all tracker changes, and commit only when dirty.\n- Apply supplied identity per commit with `git -c user.name=... -c user.email=...`; use ambient identity when omitted and never mutate global or repository config.\n- Release the write lock before delegating to `push_tickets_branch`, avoiding nested push/merge locks.\n- Delegate even when the tree is clean because already-committed local-ahead state still needs delivery.\n- In strict mode, lock, staging, or commit failures use the strict stderr/nonzero contract established by [rebar:953a-d616-52d3-4efe].\n- Keep direct `push_tickets_branch` completely push-only.\n\n## Testing\n\nUse real temporary repositories for dirty, clean/ahead, supplied-identity, and ambient-identity contracts. Add the composed operation to the existing two-clone shared concurrency suite because this task combines a locked commit with a later push/reconciliation.\n\nRED-first oracle:\n- a dirty tracker and bare origin remain uncommitted/unpublished under the current push-only API;\n- held out: supplied identity appears in `git show`; omitted identity uses the ambient repository identity;\n- held out: clean/ahead state pushes without an empty commit;\n- held out: direct `push_tickets_branch` neither stages nor commits a dirty tracker;\n- held out: competing remote and local events both survive through the two-clone barrier;\n- mutation bypassing the commit makes the dirty-tree oracle RED; removing per-command identity makes the authorship oracle RED.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A dirty tracker is committed and delivered to origin through `commit_and_push_tickets_branch`.\n- [ ] A clean but locally-ahead tracker is pushed without creating an empty commit.\n- [ ] Supplied name/email and ambient fallback identities are both proven from commit author metadata.\n- [ ] The entrypoint never mutates global or repository git identity configuration.\n- [ ] Concurrent remote and local events both remain reachable through the shared two-clone contention harness.\n- [ ] Direct `push_tickets_branch` remains push-only and preserves a dirty worktree.\n- [ ] Strict staging, commit, and lock failures follow the named stderr/nonzero contract from [rebar:953a-d616-52d3-4efe].\n- [ ] Focused pytest nodes, `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and `make test` pass.\n\n## Compatibility and rollback\n\nThe entrypoint is internal and initially unused, so it can land independently without affecting old workflows or vocabulary. Revert the later workflow-cutover change before reverting this prerequisite.","id":"2bc9-75aa-a08a-478a","parent_id":"1c1b-1da2-7ff4-4770","priority":1,"tags":["bridge","store","concurrency"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Add locked dirty-tree commit and push entrypoint"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786142461910104001,"uuid":"d00a7627-bdd8-4492-a8ea-95c9881e0eca"}